  cottage: ['Night one to day three', 'A 9 × 7 half-timber cottage: cobblestone plinth, spruce frame, light birch panels, dark oak roof. The east gable is kept plain on purpose: the workshop attaches there in the next stage.'],
  homestead: ['Week one', 'A workshop under a lean-to roof against the east gable: furnaces, smoker, blast furnace and barrels, with its own door and a doorway into the cottage. Nothing from night one is torn down.'],
  inn: ['Stage 4: the village quarter', 'The cottage roof comes off and a second floor goes on, overhanging the front and back by one block (jettying), with carved corbels underneath and lanterns by the door. Guest beds upstairs, reached by a ladder.'],
